        "contents": [
          {
            "uri": "campus://policies/hostel-rules",
            "text": "# Campus Hostel Rules and Regulations (Academic Year 2026-2027)\n\n## 1. General Conduct\n- All residents must maintain discipline, academic decorum, and mutual respect within the hostel premises.\n- Ragging or harassment of any form is strictly prohibited under zero-tolerance campus policy.\n- Quiet study hours are observed daily from 22:00 to 06:00. Loud music or disruptive noise is prohibited during these hours.\n\n## 2. Curfew and Biometric Entry\n- The hostel main gates close at 22:30 on weekdays (Sunday through Thursday) and 23:00 on Fridays and Saturdays.\n- Residents returning after curfew must produce valid warden authorization and log their entry with security.\n- Biometric check-in is mandatory before 22:30.\n\n## 3. Visitors and Guests\n- Day visitors are permitted in designated ground-floor visitor lounges between 09:00 and 18:00 only.\n- Overnight stay of non-residents or unauthorized guests is strictly forbidden.\n- Violations incur a fine of 2,500 INR and disciplinary review.\n\n## 4. Room Maintenance and Electrical Appliances\n- High-power electrical appliances (electric heaters, induction cooktops, immersion coils) are prohibited in student rooms for fire safety.\n- Room inventory and furniture must not be altered, removed, or painted.\n\n## 5. Grievances and Medical Assistance\n- Emergency medical desk: Health Center Ext. 4444 (24/7 on call).\n- Hostel warden contact: warden-hostel@campus.edu (Office: Ground Floor, Block B).\n",
            "mimeType": "text/markdown"
          }
        ]
      },
      "jsonrpc": "2.0",
      "id": 4
    }
